  "text": "The nearest star to the sun, you can't see it. It's called Proxima Centauri, a small red dwarf. It gives out less than 1% of the sun's light. Hold up your thumb at arm's length. Close one eye, then the other. Your thumb jumps against the background. Your two eyes are a ruler. Astronomers use the same trick with the whole of Earth's orbit. Its light still takes more than four years to reach you.",
